            <ArticleTitle>Hepatic blood flow in acute myocardial ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1602-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hepatic blood flow was monitored in cats during myocardial ischemia (MI). Increased plasma CPK activity, the S-T segment of the electrocardiogram, and hepatic flow was reduced by 5 h to 40% of control. The results suggest that MI can influence organs distant from the original ischemic episode.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
